# The image needs the jar and nothing else; see the Dockerfile.
src
pom.xml

# WORTH KNOWING, because the Python version of this quickstart gets a guard here that Java cannot
# have. There, local_identity.py is excluded from the build context, so setting
# DIAGRID_QUICKSTART_IDENTITY=local on a container raises ImportError and the app refuses to start
# rather than quietly trusting tokens it minted itself. Here LocalIdentityIssuer is compiled into
# target/*.jar before the image is built, so no exclusion in this file can reach it. The guards are
# the opt-in environment variable and the WARNING the issuer logs on every start. The README says
# so; prose is a weaker guard than a missing file, and pretending otherwise would be worse.
